<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolt</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cabanagem</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1835–1840</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Cabanagem was a popular revolt in the province of Grão-Pará in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amazon">Amazon</a> region of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a>, lasting from 1835 to 1840. It was one of several rebellions of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/regency-period-brazil">Regency period</a> and is estimated to have killed 30,000 to 40,000 people. It illustrated how close the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazilian-empire">Brazilian Empire</a> came to disintegration before <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pedro-ii-of-brazil">Pedro II</a>'s reign brought stability.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cabanagem.jpg" alt="Cabanagem" width="320" height="219" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Desconhecida · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cabanagem_Bel%C3%A9m_1835.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
